+# Santa Fe Weekend Plan
+
+## Trip Snapshot
+
+Two adults will spend Friday, October 8 through Sunday, October 10, 2027 in Santa Fe, staying two nights at Casa Railyard. Northern Star trains provide the inbound and return journeys, and the trip uses short walks plus the hotel shuttle without a rental car.
+
+## Booking Checklist
+
+1. Reserve round-trip seats on Northern Star trains 201 and 206.
+2. Confirm two nights at Casa Railyard.
+3. Reserve the 10:00 a.m. timed entry at the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum.
+4. Make dinner reservations at Terra & Sage and Juniper Kitchen.
+
+## Friday — Arrival and Railyard
+
+| Time | Plan | Transit |
+|---|---|---|
+| 10:20 a.m. | Arrive at Santa Fe Depot. | Meet the hotel shuttle. |
+| 10:30 a.m. | Leave the depot for Casa Railyard. | Hotel shuttle, 10 minutes. |
+| 10:45 a.m. | Drop bags at Casa Railyard. | Arrive by shuttle. |
+| 11:15 a.m. | Eat the vegetarian roasted squash bowl at Green Chile Table. | Walk 6 minutes from the hotel. |
+| 12:30 p.m. | Spend 75 minutes on the walking-light Railyard Art Walk. | Walk 8 minutes from lunch. |
+| 3:00–5:30 p.m. | Check in and take a seated rest at Casa Railyard. | Walk 8 minutes from the Railyard. |
+| 6:30 p.m. | Have vegetarian blue-corn enchiladas at Terra & Sage. | Hotel shuttle, 12 minutes. |
+
+## Saturday — Museums and Canyon Road
+
+| Time | Plan | Transit |
+|---|---|---|
+| 8:30 a.m. | Have vegetarian oatmeal and fruit at Casa Railyard. | Stay at the hotel. |
+| 10:00 a.m. | Visit the Georgia O'Keeffe Museum for the 90-minute walking-light visit. | Hotel shuttle, 10 minutes. |
+| 12:15 p.m. | Have the vegetarian chile relleno plate at Plaza Cafe. | Walk 8 minutes from the museum. |
+| 2:00–3:30 p.m. | Follow the Canyon Road gallery loop, the day's walking-intensive activity. | Hotel shuttle, 10 minutes. |
+| 4:30–6:00 p.m. | Take a seated rest at Casa Railyard. | Hotel shuttle, 12 minutes. |
+| 7:00 p.m. | Have vegetarian mushroom posole at Juniper Kitchen. | Hotel shuttle, 9 minutes. |
+
+## Sunday — Plaza and Departure
+
+| Time | Plan | Transit |
+|---|---|---|
+| 9:00 a.m. | Check out and store the bags at Casa Railyard. | Stay at the hotel. |
+| 9:30–10:45 a.m. | Join the walking-intensive Plaza Architecture Walk. | Hotel shuttle, 10 minutes. |
+| 12:00 p.m. | Have the vegetarian bean-and-corn tostada at Cactus Bloom. | Walk 5 minutes from the Plaza. |
+| 1:30 p.m. | Spend 45 minutes at the walking-light Railyard Park overlook. | Hotel shuttle, 12 minutes. |
+| 3:00–4:30 p.m. | Take a seated rest in the Casa Railyard lounge. | Walk 6 minutes from the park. |
+| 4:30 p.m. | Collect the stored bags. | Remain at Casa Railyard. |
+| 5:00 p.m. | Leave for Santa Fe Depot. | Hotel shuttle, 10 minutes. |
+| 6:05 p.m. | Depart on Northern Star train 206. | Board at the depot. |
+
+## Practical Notes
+
+The vegetarian choices are built into every named meal: Green Chile Table and Terra & Sage on Friday, the hotel breakfast, Plaza Cafe, and Juniper Kitchen on Saturday, and Cactus Bloom on Sunday. Confirm those preparations when making the two dinner reservations.
+
+For the traveler's knee fatigue, keep every walk to 15 minutes or less, use the hotel shuttle for the longer transfers shown, and protect each afternoon rest block. The plan limits Saturday and Sunday to one walking-intensive activity apiece; the other visits are walking-light. Pack a light layer, sun protection, comfortable walking shoes, and a refillable water bottle.
